%U A396051 2688808220403,1,42121049526188,90367156,701753968883466,12642,12399466309422845,1,231504809071175967
%N A396051 Number of fixed-content bracelets of length 2*n, summed over all integer partitions of 2*n, whose mirror image is a non-identity rotation, with no linear-palindrome representative and a nontrivial rotational symmetry.
%C A396051 For an integer partition lambda = (lambda_1, ..., lambda_k) of 2*n, use k colors and require color i to occur lambda_i times. The profile lambda is fixed in weakly decreasing order; color relabelings are not additional objects for the same lambda. This is the strongly normal fixed-content convention.
%C A396051 This sequence counts bracelets represented by a circular word X such that (1) the mirror image of X is a non-identity rotation of X, (2) no rotation of X is a linear palindrome, and (3) some non-identity rotation fixes X. Equivalently, this is the periodic S0 class in the refined fixed-content bracelet atlas.
%C A396051 Every counted object has a unique primitive root U of even length 2*d, where d is a positive divisor of n with d<n. The primitive orbit of U has full rotational period, is closed under reversal, and has no linear-palindrome representative; it is therefore counted by A396632(d). Conversely, raising every object counted by A396632(d) to the power n/d gives one object counted here.
%C A396051 The class vanishes in odd underlying length. The sequence is indexed by half-length n and starts at n=2, because the value at n=1 is zero.
%C A396051 For prime n, a(n)=1.
%H A396051 Andrea Cutri, <a href="/A396051/b396051.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 2..40</a>.
%H A396051 Andrea Cutri, <a href="https://github.com/aku-79/oeis-refined-atlas/blob/main/programs/a396051.py">Python program</a>.
%F A396051 a(n) = Sum_{d | n, d < n} A396632(d).
%F A396051 a(p) = 1 for every prime.
%e A396051 For n=4 the positive divisors d<4 are 1 and 2, so a(4) = A396632(1) + A396632(2) = 1 + 2 = 3. The primitive representative 01 of length 2 gives 01010101, while the two primitive length-4 objects represented by 0001 and 0102 give 00010001 and 01020102. Each resulting bracelet has a nontrivial rotational symmetry, its mirror image is a non-identity rotation, and none of its distinct rotations is a linear palindrome.
%Y A396051 Cf. A005651, A072605, A213943, A395436, A396085, A396630, A396631, A396632.
